{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>אַף חֹבֵב עַמִּים כָּל קְדֹשָׁיו בְּיָדֶךָ וגו׳.</b> He says: even at the time when the Holy One, blessed be He, shows affection to the nations, nevertheless the affection for Israel is not comparable to the affection for the nations — for ״כָּל קְדֹשָׁיו״ means Israel, קֹדֶשׁ יִשְׂרָאֵל לַה׳ (Jeremiah 2:3) — they are ״בְּיָדֶךָ״, governed directly by Your hand, blessed be He, for You did not hand them over to the governance of the celestial array. ״וְהֵם״, that is, the nations, ״תֻּכּוּ לְרַגְלֶיךָ״, for they are handed over to the celestial array which is under His feet, blessed be He. And reason dictates this, for the nations are like a burden and a load regarding the word of HaShem — this is what it says: ״יִשָּׂא מִדַּבְּרֹתֶיךָ״, that they will bear all Your words, for like a heavy burden they are too heavy for them (Psalms 38:5). But Israel are not so; rather, ״תּוֹרָה צִוָּה לָנוּ מֹשֶׁה מוֹרָשָׁה קְהִלַּת יַעֲקֹב״ — even though Moses commanded us for that generation, nevertheless it is an inheritance for every assembly of Jacob in every generation; all of them stood and accepted upon themselves to bequeath and hand down the Torah to their children after them. And all this indicates the opposite — that the word of HaShem is not a burden upon them; rather, they stood and accepted it upon themselves and upon their seed with joy to do it." "And he said further: ״יִשָּׂא מִדַּבְּרֹתֶיךָ״ — even Your good word which they hear from Your mouth is upon the nations like a burden. But Israel are not so; rather, they say: Even the Torah that Moses commanded us, which we did not hear from the mouth of the Almighty — nevertheless it is an inheritance for every assembly of Jacob. Therefore ״וַיְהִי בִישֻׁרוּן מֶלֶךְ״ — specifically in Israel was Elohim known as King, but not among the nations."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :register {:flags {1 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {1 "The phrases יִשָּׂא מִדַּבְּרֹתֶיךָ, תּוֹרָה צִוָּה לָנוּ מֹשֶׁה מוֹרָשָׁה קְהִלַּת יַעֲקֹב, and וַיְהִי בִישֻׁרוּן מֶלֶךְ are all citations from nearby verses in the same chapter (Deuteronomy 33) left unaddressed by the author."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:25.283387985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}